{"output":"I'll start by discovering the tools on the two MCP servers.\n\nI processed all 25 open `warranty` claims in id order. Each got one comment and a status. `/app/STATUS.json` is written with status `success`. I didn't re-read the tickets or stock afterwards. I relied on the success responses from each call.\n\n- **Shipped, 15 claims, resolved:**\n  - I shipped 14 new replacements: #1107, #1108, #1113, #1114, #1117, #1120, #1122, #1123, #1124, #1126, #1127, #1133, #1134 and #1135. Their adjustments are `adj-107` to `adj-120`.\n  - #1125 had already been shipped by a colleague, so I shipped nothing and answered it with `adj-102`.\n- **Not covered, 8 claims, closed:**\n  - Warranty expired: #1106, #1110, #1115, #1116 and #1118.\n  - Product line excluded: #1121 and #1128.\n  - Serial already replaced: #1132. Its serial was shipped under #1103, so I shipped nothing.\n- **Backordered, 1 claim, pending:** #1130 needs 2 units of PT-1209, and neither east nor west holds 2.\n- **Duplicate, 1 claim:** #1131 is a duplicate of #1108, set to `duplicate`.\n\nA few results depend on edge cases:\n- #1120 is covered because it was created on the last day of its 24-month warranty (2026-09-11).\n- #1127 ships the successor PT-1219, because PT-1203 is discontinued.\n- #1133 ships from north, because west ran out after #1107 and north holds the most of the other warehouses.\n- #1122 was only transferred between warehouses by a colleague, not shipped, so I shipped it from north.","final_output":"I processed all 25 open warranty claims in id order. Each got one comment and a status. /app/STATUS.json is written with status success. I didn't re-read the tickets or stock afterwards. I relied on the success responses from each call.\n\n- Shipped, 15 claims, resolved:\n  - I shipped 14 new replacements: #1107, #1108, #1113, #1114, #1117, #1120, #1122, #1123, #1124, #1126, #1127, #1133, #1134 and #1135. Their adjustments are adj-107 to adj-120.\n  - #1125 had already been shipped by a c